   <narrative xml:lang="EN">United Nations Industrial Development Organization</narrative>
  </reporting-org>
  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HCFC phase-out management plan (stage II) in Somalia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">In Somalia the servicing sector is quite large and scattered across the country. The refrigerants used in the servicing is mainly HCFC-22, R-410A, R407C &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; R404A. During the survey it has been observed that the consumption of HCFC-22 is in the servicing of domestic air-conditioning, commercial air conditioning, transport refrigeration, large commercial refrigeration and industrial refrigeration. The project was approved at the 95th ExCom in 2024 and it will last until 2030. Somalia will commit itself to a full reduction of HCFC consumption, notwithstanding the provisions for the so-called servicing tail of 2.5 percent that may last until 2040, according to the relevant decisions of the Meeting of the Parties to the Montreal Protocol.</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org role="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Montreal Protocol</narrative>
  </participating-org>
